<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>AI Summer Camp - Task 3</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/task3.css">
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.4.0/css/all.min.css">
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="task-card">
            <!-- Header Section -->
            <div class="header-section">
                <a href="/lobby" class="back-btn">
                    <i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i>
                    <%= user.role === 'INSTRUCTOR' ? 'Back to Leaderboard' : 'Back to Lobby' %>
                </a>
                <a href="/logout" class="logout-btn">
                    <i class="fas fa-sign-out-alt"></i>
                    Logout
                </a>
            </div>

            <div class="task-header">
                <h1 class="task-title">Step 1: Categorical Classification Challenge</h1>
                <p class="task-subtitle">Learning how collected features enable multi-class classification</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Introduction Section -->
            <div class="intro-section">
                <h2 class="section-title">Multi-Class Classification</h2>
                <div class="intro-content">
                    <div class="intro-text">
                        <p class="description-text">
                            Now that you've understood feature extraction, let's explore <strong>categorical classification</strong>. 
                            Remember: those features you extracted in previous tasks weren't just for observation, they were the actual 
                            <span class="highlight">input data</span> that gets fed into machine learning models.
                        </p>
                        <p class="description-text">
                            AI systems don't see objects as whole entities. Instead, they receive <strong>descriptive features</strong> 
                            as separate data points: color=red, texture=smooth, etc. These feature combinations allow models to distinguish 
                            between multiple categories.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Training Data Section -->
            <div class="training-section">
                <h2 class="section-title">Training Examples</h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">Study these three ingredient types and their unique feature combinations</p>
                <div class="training-grid">
                    <div class="training-item firestone">
                        <h3 class="item-title">Firestone</h3>
                        <div class="ingredient-icon">
                            <i class="fas fa-fire"></i>
                        </div>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <h4 class="features-title">Key Features:</h4>
                            <ul class="features">
                                <li><strong>Color:</strong> Red with orange glow</li>
                                <li><strong>Texture:</strong> Jagged and crystalline</li>
                                <li><strong>Aura:</strong> Fiery and warm energy</li>
                                <li><strong>Element:</strong> Fire-based magical properties</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="training-item waterleaf">
                        <h3 class="item-title">Waterleaf</h3>
                        <div class="ingredient-icon">
                            <i class="fas fa-tint"></i>
                        </div>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <h4 class="features-title">Key Features:</h4>
                            <ul class="features">
                                <li><strong>Color:</strong> Blue with aqua shimmer</li>
                                <li><strong>Texture:</strong> Smooth and flowing</li>
                                <li><strong>Aura:</strong> Cool and calming energy</li>
                                <li><strong>Element:</strong> Water-based magical properties</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="training-item windwhisper">
                        <h3 class="item-title">Windwhisper</h3>
                        <div class="ingredient-icon">
                            <i class="fas fa-wind"></i>
                        </div>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <h4 class="features-title">Key Features:</h4>
                            <ul class="features">
                                <li><strong>Color:</strong> Gray with silver streaks</li>
                                <li><strong>Texture:</strong> Light and ethereal</li>
                                <li><strong>Aura:</strong> Breezy and floating energy</li>
                                <li><strong>Element:</strong> Air-based magical properties</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Testing Section -->
            <div class="testing-section">
                <h2 class="section-title">Step 2: Classify These Mystery Ingredients</h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">Use the feature combinations to determine which category each ingredient belongs to</p>
                
                <div class="testing-grid">
                    <div class="test-item">
                        <div class="ingredient-icon mystery">
                            <i class="fas fa-question"></i>
                        </div>
                        <label for="answer1" class="test-label">Mystery Ingredient A</label>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <p class="observed-features"><strong>Observed Features:</strong></p>
                            <ul class="feature-tags">
                                <li>Color: Blue</li>
                                <li>Texture: Smooth</li>
                                <li>Aura: Cool</li>
                                <li>Element: Water</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <select id="answer1" class="answer-select">
                            <option value="">Choose classification...</option>
                            <option value="Firestone">Firestone</option>
                            <option value="Waterleaf">Waterleaf</option>
                            <option value="Windwhisper">Windwhisper</option>
                        </select>
                    </div>
                    <div class="test-item">
                        <div class="ingredient-icon mystery">
                            <i class="fas fa-question"></i>
                        </div>
                        <label for="answer2" class="test-label">Mystery Ingredient B</label>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <p class="observed-features"><strong>Observed Features:</strong></p>
                            <ul class="feature-tags">
                                <li>Color: Red</li>
                                <li>Texture: Jagged</li>
                                <li>Aura: Fiery</li>
                                <li>Element: Fire</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <select id="answer2" class="answer-select">
                            <option value="">Choose classification...</option>
                            <option value="Firestone">Firestone</option>
                            <option value="Waterleaf">Waterleaf</option>
                            <option value="Windwhisper">Windwhisper</option>
                        </select>
                    </div>
                    <div class="test-item">
                        <div class="ingredient-icon mystery">
                            <i class="fas fa-question"></i>
                        </div>
                        <label for="answer3" class="test-label">Mystery Ingredient C</label>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <p class="observed-features"><strong>Observed Features:</strong></p>
                            <ul class="feature-tags">
                                <li>Color: Gray</li>
                                <li>Texture: Light</li>
                                <li>Aura: Breezy</li>
                                <li>Element: Air</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <select id="answer3" class="answer-select">
                            <option value="">Choose classification...</option>
                            <option value="Firestone">Firestone</option>
                            <option value="Waterleaf">Waterleaf</option>
                            <option value="Windwhisper">Windwhisper</option>
                        </select>
                    </div>
                </div>
                
                <div class="accuracy-section">
                    <p class="accuracy-explanation">
                        <strong>Real AI Challenge:</strong> Machine learning models are never 100% certain. They calculate 
                        <span class="highlight">accuracy percentages</span> and choose the highest probability. 
                        Sometimes features don't perfectly match any single category:
                    </p>
                    
                    <div class="test-item mixed-item">
                        <div class="ingredient-icon mystery">
                            <i class="fas fa-question-circle"></i>
                        </div>
                        <label for="answer4" class="test-label">Mystery Ingredient D (Mixed Features)</label>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <p class="observed-features"><strong>Observed Features:</strong></p>
                            <ul class="feature-tags mixed-tags">
                                <li>Color: Blue-Gray</li>
                                <li>Texture: Smooth-Light</li>
                                <li>Aura: Cool-Breezy</li>
                                <li>Element: Water-Air</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mixed-analysis">
                            <p class="analysis-prompt">This ingredient shows features from multiple classes. Analyze which two classes it's mixing:</p>
                            <div class="mixture-selection">
                                <label for="mixture1">First Class (Higher Probability):</label>
                                <select id="mixture1" class="mixture-select">
                                    <option value="">Choose first class...</option>
                                    <option value="Waterleaf">Waterleaf</option>
                                    <option value="Windwhisper">Windwhisper</option>
                                    <option value="Firestone">Firestone</option>
                                </select>
                                
                                <label for="mixture2">Second Class (Lower Probability):</label>
                                <select id="mixture2" class="mixture-select">
                                    <option value="">Choose second class...</option>
                                    <option value="Waterleaf">Waterleaf</option>
                                    <option value="Windwhisper">Windwhisper</option>
                                    <option value="Firestone">Firestone</option>
                                </select>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                
                 <div class="submit-section">
                    <button id="checkButton" class="submit-btn">
                        <span><%= user.role === 'INSTRUCTOR' ? 'Show Solution' : 'Check My Answers' %></span>
                        <div class="btn-icon">
                            <i class="fas fa-<%= user.role === 'INSTRUCTOR' ? 'eye' : 'check' %>"></i>
                        </div>
                    </button>
                </div>
                <script> const userRole = "<%= user.role %>"; </script>
                
            </div>

            <!-- Feedback Section -->
            <div id="feedback" class="feedback-section hidden">
                <h3 class="feedback-title">Your Results</h3>
                <div id="score-display" class="score-display"></div>
                <ul id="feedback-list" class="feedback-list"></ul>
                
                <!-- Educational Explanation -->
                <div id="explanation" class="explanation-section">
                    <h4 class="explanation-title">What Just Happened?</h4>
                    <p class="explanation-text">
                        You just performed <strong>categorical classification</strong>! Instead of choosing between just two options, 
                        you used feature combinations to sort items into multiple distinct categories. This is exactly how AI systems 
                        handle complex real-world classification tasks.
                    </p>
                    <p class="explanation-text">
                        By collecting and analyzing multiple features (color, texture, aura, element), you could distinguish between 
                        three different classes. <strong>Machine learning algorithms</strong> use this same approach to classify 
                        emails as spam/important/promotional, identify different species of animals, or categorize medical diagnoses.
                    </p>
                    <p class="explanation-text">
                        The fourth ingredient demonstrated a crucial AI concept: <strong>accuracy and uncertainty</strong>. When features 
                        don't perfectly match a single category, AI models calculate <span class="highlight">confidence percentages</span> 
                        for each possible class. Your mixture analysis mimicked how real AI systems handle ambiguous data by weighing 
                        different feature combinations and assigning probability scores.
                    </p>
                    <p class="explanation-text">
                        In real-world applications, AI systems rarely give 100% certainty. Instead, they provide accuracy percentages like 
                        "85% confident this is a cat" or "70% chance this email is spam." This probabilistic approach allows AI to make 
                        informed decisions even when data is unclear or incomplete.
                    </p>
                </div>
                
                <div class="next-section">
                    <button id="nextButton" class="next-btn">
                        <span>Continue to Next Task</span>
                        <div class="btn-icon">
                            <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i>
                        </div>
                    </button>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script src="/js/task3.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
